  ok   -- an empty file -> UNMEASURED and fired=False, which means NOTHING
  ok   -- a turn that called no tool -> UNMEASURED ('nothing to look at', not 'no repeats')

agent_reuse_gap: fires on delegable content, silent on orchestration
  ok   -- POSITIVE: 12 CONTENT turns, no dispatch -> gap at least 12, longest run 12, FIRED
  ok   -- NEGATIVE (the one that matters): 12 ORCHESTRATION turns -- the SAME 12-turn gap -- not fired, because alm#833 says those turns structurally cannot move
  ok   -- NEGATIVE: a dispatch at turn 10 of 12 -> gap of 1, not fired
  ok   -- BOUNDARY: a gap of 12 does not fire at threshold 12 and does at 11
  ok   -- raising min_content_run to 99 makes the same window not delegable-looking, so the long gap alone does not fire -- both halves are load-bearing
  ok   -- no threshold -> NOT COMPUTED, with the gap still reported
  ok   -- a FULL read reports its gap exactly (12), a WINDOWED read reports it as a floor (at least 6) -- because only the latter can be hiding an older dispatch

F2: the ten mutants that used to survive this suite
  ok   -- a pair of commands sitting EXACTLY on the 0.60 retry threshold exists (jaccard 0.600) -- the boundary is reachable, so it can be tested
  ok   -- and a pair AT the threshold is treated as a retry and is NOT mergeable (examined 1, mergeable 0) -- `>=` not `>`
  ok   -- a two-tool turn next to a single-Bash turn contributes NO pair; only the single/single pair is examined (1, not 2)
  ok   -- a TEXT-ONLY assistant turn between two Bash turns is a barrier: 0 pairs examined, so nothing is mergeable across it (got 0)
