  ok   -- and it FIRES on that, with `measure` taken from the in-span window (3) -- so deleting repeated_in_spans now goes red
  ok   -- a CONTENT run of EXACTLY 3 is delegable-looking at the 3-turn break-even and fires -- `>=` not `>`
  ok   -- 5 main + 5 sidechain turns: the gap counts the 5 MAIN turns (5) and does not fire at a threshold of 5; counting the sidechain's own turns would make it 10 and fire
  ok   -- a turn with no tool call classifies as REPORT, not CONTENT
  ok   -- and a REPORT turn inside a run BREAKS it: longest run 2, not the 4 CONTENT turns either side of it, so the 3-turn gate stays shut
  ok   -- a `since` window that cut past line 0 reports head_complete=False -- its oldest turn may be a fragment, and saying True would be a promise it cannot keep
  ok   -- while a full read of the same file reports head_complete=True
  ok   -- every pair of windowing arguments is refused (3 of 3)
  ok   -- an offset inside an unterminated final line returns NO bytes and an offset of EOF (got b'', 60) -- there is no complete line at or after it
  ok   -- while an offset inside the FIRST line still returns the unterminated tail, because a complete line boundary does exist after it

