  ok   -- asking for 3 turn(s) of a transcript that replays EVERY id returns exactly 3, at read_fraction 1.000. An identity-keyed cut returns 4 for every one of these, because the newest ids' FIRST appearance is in the first half -- it reports head_complete=True while silently answering a different question
  ok   -- when the computed read position is EXACTLY a line start (553), the read begins there. Without the one-byte look-back that proves it is a boundary, this case cannot be told from 'mid-line' and the loop falls back to offset 0 -- the whole file, which is the saving this library exists to make
